From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 16:21:42 +0000
Subject: pinctrl: equilibrium: allow building for the Intel MIPS platform

The Equilibrium pin controller is not exclusive to the Lightning
Mountain (x86) SoC: the Intel MIPS (xRX500/GRX350) family carries the
very same IP block. Its PINPAD and GPIO register maps are byte-identical
to the ones this driver programs -- REG_PMX_BASE/PUEN/PDEN/SRC/DCC0/
DCC1/OD/AVAIL at 0x00/0x80..0x98 and GPIO OUT/IN/DIR/IRN*/OUTSET/OUTCLR/
DIRSET/DIRCLR at 0x00..0x4C -- as can be verified against the vendor
xrx500 pinctrl driver in the AVM 4.9 tree (drivers/pinctrl/
pinctrl-equilibrium.{c,h}, bound there to "intel,pinctrl-xrx500").

Extend the dependency so PINCTRL_EQUILIBRIUM is selectable on
INTEL_MIPS, mirroring what "serial: lantiq: allow building for the Intel
MIPS platform", earlier in this series, did for the shared ASC UART.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/pinctrl/Kconfig b/drivers/pinctrl/Kconfig
index 80db4195a559..3de5abdd8e0b 100644
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/Kconfig
@@ -230,7 +230,7 @@ config PINCTRL_EP93XX
 config PINCTRL_EQUILIBRIUM
 	tristate "Generic pinctrl and GPIO driver for Intel Lightning Mountain SoC"
 	depends on OF && HAS_IOMEM
-	depends on X86 || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on X86 || INTEL_MIPS || COMPILE_TEST
 	select PINMUX
 	select PINCONF
 	select GPIOLIB
